WEBVTT

00:00:00.760 --> 00:00:01.990
Classified?

00:00:02.630 --> 00:00:06.710
If I attempted to acquire those records,

00:00:07.190 --> 00:00:12.420
the Justice and Executive would 
suspect something has happened.

00:00:14.460 --> 00:00:15.530
I see.

00:00:16.370 --> 00:00:18.160
White Sand Prison...

00:00:19.330 --> 00:00:24.750
is heavily guarded on the outside, 
but not so much on the inside.

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.940
You might be able to sneak a peek.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:31.760
If you can sneak in, that is.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:15.400
<b>Mystery 12 "The Cobweb"</b>

00:02:11.650 --> 00:02:14.350
<i>Like the Legislator's place, 
the doors of White Sand Prison</i>

00:02:14.350 --> 00:02:16.530
<i>can be opened from the inside,</i>

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.780
<i>but not from the outside.</i>

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:22.080
<i>No, I shouldn't break in.</i>

00:02:22.080 --> 00:02:23.450
Itsuki?

00:02:24.500 --> 00:02:29.480
Koura. I was just thinking about picking 
up some medicine at the Kiyakudo.

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:33.110
Oh, you're early this time.

00:02:33.510 --> 00:02:35.720
I happened to be in the neighborhood.

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.050
Well, that's no good.

00:02:38.950 --> 00:02:43.390
I'm making a delivery to the 
Justice at White Sand Prison.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:45.390
White Sand Prison?

00:02:45.880 --> 00:02:49.390
Since you're here, could you walk me there?

00:02:50.450 --> 00:02:53.520
Why do I have to walk you there?

00:02:53.520 --> 00:02:54.990
Why not?

00:02:54.990 --> 00:02:58.280
I can't give you your medicine 
until I get back, anyway.

00:02:58.800 --> 00:03:00.540
A delivery, you said?

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.030
Is the Justice sick or something?

00:03:03.320 --> 00:03:07.210
He ran out of the anesthetic he 
uses when torturing prisoners.

00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:11.040
I made a stronger batch for him this time.

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:13.270
I-I see...

00:03:15.560 --> 00:03:20.300
Thank you for bringing it all the way here.

00:03:20.600 --> 00:03:23.220
Please, come in.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.720
Would you like to go in with me, Itsuki?

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:28.010
No, I'll wait here.

00:03:28.010 --> 00:03:31.230
Then I'll be right back.

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:47.830
<i>I believe the records are at the 
Justice's White Sand Prison.</i>

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.890
<i>What am I doing?</i>

00:04:23.620 --> 00:04:26.870
<i>If I can just find the records 
related to the mundane world...</i>

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:28.740
<i>Is this it?</i>

00:04:31.580 --> 00:04:34.080
<b>Mononokean</b>

00:04:35.140 --> 00:04:36.080
Here you go.

00:04:36.630 --> 00:04:38.990
Why, thank you.

00:04:38.990 --> 00:04:42.540
This is the anesthetic you requested.

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:45.820
Thank you.

00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:48.970
Where's the Justice? Is he out?

00:04:48.970 --> 00:04:50.920
I'm sorry,

00:04:50.920 --> 00:04:54.980
but unfortunately, the Justice 
has a guest at the moment.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:04:59.770
Your library is that way, isn't it?

00:05:03.480 --> 00:05:05.320
Yeah, it is.

00:05:11.860 --> 00:05:15.880
<i>A blond-haired, golden-eyed 
human who used his influence...</i>

00:05:20.590 --> 00:05:23.380
<i>One who committed taboo acts 
in the mundane world...</i>

00:05:27.090 --> 00:05:32.010
He was a dangerous fellow who 
killed and imprisoned yokai.

00:05:37.020 --> 00:05:42.020
<b>"Sakae"</b>

00:05:37.670 --> 00:05:38.920
<i>Sakae...</i>

00:05:39.510 --> 00:05:40.940
<i>Ashiya Sakae.</i>

00:05:42.530 --> 00:05:44.530
When I asked him who he was,

00:05:45.400 --> 00:05:48.320
he said he was an employee of the Mononokean.

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:51.520
This must be him.

00:05:51.520 --> 00:05:54.220
Ashiya Sakae was the Mononokean's...

00:05:58.000 --> 00:05:59.210
<i>Shoot!</i>

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.670
<i>Did Abeno-san go to the Underworld again?</i>

00:06:08.710 --> 00:06:10.680
Oh, Zenko.

00:06:11.830 --> 00:06:15.180
Hanae, do you have a minute?

00:06:16.070 --> 00:06:16.940
Yeah.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:20.150
A shrine?

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:25.130
It's an old shrine, but rumor 
has it there's something there.

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:30.680
My dad spoke with the president 
of the neighborhood association.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:33.410
Like that time with the Bon Festival dance?

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:39.120
Since then, he's assumed my 
dad has supernatural powers.

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:41.290
Supernatural?

00:06:41.290 --> 00:06:44.290
But he really doesn't seem 
to like that kind of thing.

00:06:49.220 --> 00:06:52.220
Okay. I'll talk to Abeno-san tomorrow.

00:06:55.860 --> 00:06:58.140
Aw, just Ashiya?

00:06:58.880 --> 00:07:01.310
Yahiko, did you just get back?

00:07:01.310 --> 00:07:05.400
I was gonna ask Haruitsuki to play 
with me again, if he were here.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.650
Abeno-san seems to be busy.

00:07:08.650 --> 00:07:09.880
Whatever.

00:07:09.880 --> 00:07:13.450
Haruitsuki played with 
me a lot the other day.

00:07:14.310 --> 00:07:15.580
Really?

00:07:15.580 --> 00:07:19.410
Yeah, in exchange for me 
transforming into Ashiya Sakae.

00:07:22.200 --> 00:07:25.790
You could've had an employee 
deliver it to you.

00:07:26.190 --> 00:07:28.220
I can't do that.

00:07:28.220 --> 00:07:33.550
You know it's forbidden to remove 
documents from this library.

00:07:33.550 --> 00:07:34.800
<i>The Executive...</i>

00:07:35.480 --> 00:07:37.440
You're too serious.

00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:41.350
You could take them if I allowed it.

00:07:48.090 --> 00:07:53.030
Justice, where are the 
documents I'm looking for?

00:07:53.030 --> 00:07:57.840
I must finish my business quickly 
so I can return to the Birdcage.

00:07:57.840 --> 00:07:59.830
Oh, yeah.

00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:03.080
They're over here.

00:08:27.800 --> 00:08:29.860
I panicked and brought it with me.

00:08:32.840 --> 00:08:33.610
Here.

00:08:33.610 --> 00:08:35.400
Thanks for waiting.

00:08:35.400 --> 00:08:37.220
Thanks.

00:08:38.020 --> 00:08:41.100
You should've brought Ashiya with you.

00:08:41.100 --> 00:08:42.420
I will eventually.

00:08:46.980 --> 00:08:49.580
Why are you so flustered?

00:08:49.580 --> 00:08:51.450
N-No reason.

00:08:51.450 --> 00:08:56.830
I'll give you a new analeptic medicine later.

00:08:56.830 --> 00:08:58.300
No, thanks.

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:02.140
Please turn into Sakae!

00:09:02.630 --> 00:09:03.640
No.

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:04.880
Why not?

00:09:04.880 --> 00:09:07.230
Didn't you transform for Abeno-san?

00:09:07.230 --> 00:09:09.740
I'll play with you all you want, too!

00:09:09.740 --> 00:09:12.190
Hide-and-seek? Tag?

00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.820
I won't play unless Haruitsuki's with you.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.660
I'll give you candy!

00:09:18.980 --> 00:09:19.990
Candy?

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:23.750
Yeah! I'll buy whatever you want!

00:09:24.930 --> 00:09:27.130
I'll consider it if you bring me some.

00:09:33.190 --> 00:09:36.760
<i>I'm surprised Yahiko even met Sakae,</i>

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:40.840
<i>but why did Abeno-san 
want to see Sakae's form?</i>

00:09:40.840 --> 00:09:43.260
<i>He didn't even seem interested.</i>

00:09:45.770 --> 00:09:47.270
<b>Sister</b>

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:49.590
Hello?

00:09:50.050 --> 00:09:53.000
<i>Hanae, how are you?</i>

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:54.780
Good. What's up?

00:09:55.050 --> 00:09:58.080
<i>I was wondering how Mom's doing.</i>

00:09:58.080 --> 00:10:01.530
She's so energetic, it's hard 
to believe she collapsed.

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:06.090
She opened up shop the day 
she got out of the hospital.

00:10:06.500 --> 00:10:08.790
I told her to take some time off.

00:10:08.790 --> 00:10:11.920
<i>I see. That's fine, then.</i>

00:10:11.920 --> 00:10:14.300
You should've called her.

00:10:14.300 --> 00:10:15.980
<i>I'm about to.</i>

00:10:15.980 --> 00:10:19.180
<i>I thought I'd check in with you first.</i>

00:10:20.450 --> 00:10:21.800
What does that mean?

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:25.720
<i>Remember how I went to pick her 
up when she was discharged?</i>

00:10:26.600 --> 00:10:27.860
<i>Well...</i>

00:10:29.320 --> 00:10:32.000
Thank you very much.

00:10:32.000 --> 00:10:34.820
Hurry up. The taxi's waiting.

00:10:37.320 --> 00:10:41.230
They took care of me. I have to thank them.

00:10:41.230 --> 00:10:44.300
You're embarrassing them by spending 
ten minutes thanking them

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:46.170
for three days and two nights.

00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:49.880
This isn't so bad once in a while.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:51.830
It's a nice change of pace.

00:10:51.830 --> 00:10:55.190
Don't tell me you enjoyed 
being in the hospital.

00:10:56.400 --> 00:10:59.660
I came as quickly as I could. 
Put yourself in my shoes.

00:10:59.660 --> 00:11:01.340
By the way,

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:04.410
I met Hanae's friend.

00:11:05.120 --> 00:11:07.350
He was kind of like him.

00:11:15.440 --> 00:11:17.540
Like who?

00:11:17.540 --> 00:11:19.660
No, never mind.

00:11:22.160 --> 00:11:24.430
You're so carefree.

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:26.660
Do you know how worried your kids were?

00:11:30.200 --> 00:11:32.890
I should thank Sakae-kun.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:34.460
Where did that come from?

00:11:35.240 --> 00:11:39.970
He left me such a kind family.

00:11:46.310 --> 00:11:50.090
<i>She had never talked about him before.</i>

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:57.520
<i>I've been strangely curious 
about it since I got back.</i>

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.080
Don't worry.

00:11:59.080 --> 00:12:01.200
She's totally her usual self.

00:12:01.200 --> 00:12:02.360
<i>That's fine, then.</i>

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:04.540
<i>I'll call Mom now.</i>

00:12:04.540 --> 00:12:08.910
Let her know I'm on my way home.

00:12:08.910 --> 00:12:10.200
<i>Okay.</i>

00:12:17.210 --> 00:12:20.070
<b>Caution
Railroad Crossing</b>

00:12:20.070 --> 00:12:23.050
<b>Generational Grave</b>

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:23.050
Please, Yahiko-sama!

00:12:23.420 --> 00:12:24.680
No.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:26.320
What?!

00:12:26.320 --> 00:12:28.510
Yahiko, please transform!

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:31.520
Tomorrow.

00:12:31.520 --> 00:12:33.600
You've been saying that for three days now!

00:12:33.600 --> 00:12:35.740
You're never gonna transform, are you?!

00:12:35.740 --> 00:12:38.730
And every time, you make 
me bring cream puffs,

00:12:38.730 --> 00:12:40.800
pudding, rice dumplings, and dorayaki!

00:12:40.800 --> 00:12:42.530
Because of you, I'm broke!

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:44.910
I want melon next time.

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:51.470
I'm leaving for today, but next 
time, you'd better transform!

00:12:51.470 --> 00:12:52.810
You'd better not forget!

00:12:53.510 --> 00:12:54.560
Abeno-san!

00:12:54.560 --> 00:12:56.240
Why are you surprised?

00:12:56.240 --> 00:12:57.420
I'm right on time.

00:12:57.420 --> 00:13:01.610
Oh, right. I got here a little early, 
so I was playing with Yahiko.

00:13:02.780 --> 00:13:04.420
Thanks for coming.

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:07.880
It's fine. Ashiya more or less filled me in.

00:13:07.880 --> 00:13:09.820
Haruitsuki, let's play!

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:11.310
I have work.

00:13:11.310 --> 00:13:12.860
Aw...

00:13:12.860 --> 00:13:15.370
Yahiko, you were in the 
middle of cleaning the yard.

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:16.960
I won't give you a snack.

00:13:16.960 --> 00:13:18.710
Oh, right!

00:13:18.710 --> 00:13:20.320
Bye, Haruitsuki!

00:13:20.320 --> 00:13:22.890
Ashiya, feel free to stop by anytime.

00:13:22.890 --> 00:13:25.000
Y-Yeah, see you later.

00:13:26.050 --> 00:13:29.120
What do I want after melon?

00:13:29.520 --> 00:13:31.880
<i>He's going to make me feed him forever?</i>

00:13:34.560 --> 00:13:38.120
<i>When did they become such good friends?</i>

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:43.630
Moaning, huh?

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.010
Could it be a stray dog?

00:13:45.480 --> 00:13:49.530
Some witnesses saw red 
eyes glowing in the brush.

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:52.680
We'll go check it out.

00:13:53.930 --> 00:13:54.900
Yeah.

00:13:59.880 --> 00:14:01.200
What?

00:14:01.200 --> 00:14:02.520
Nothing.

00:14:02.520 --> 00:14:03.530
Say it.

00:14:03.900 --> 00:14:04.530
Huh?

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.650
There's something you want to tell me.

00:14:06.650 --> 00:14:09.580
Well, our team has been together for years.

00:14:09.580 --> 00:14:14.030
You always have something to say 
to me when you make that face!

00:14:14.030 --> 00:14:17.040
And it hasn't been years, 
and we're not a team!

00:14:17.040 --> 00:14:18.680
Um,

00:14:19.640 --> 00:14:21.290
it's about Sakae.

00:14:28.020 --> 00:14:30.800
<i>Huh... So you really snuck in.</i>

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:35.810
Having a look was fine, but taking 
a book was not a good idea.

00:14:36.230 --> 00:14:39.500
I know. I didn't mean to take it.

00:14:41.110 --> 00:14:43.320
There was a little accident.

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:48.280
I'll keep this.

00:14:48.280 --> 00:14:53.160
It's no big deal if a book or two 
goes missing for a little while.

00:14:54.760 --> 00:14:57.440
You never seem to be aware 
of your own position.

00:14:57.440 --> 00:14:58.680
I am.

00:14:59.700 --> 00:15:02.460
Because of my position, I believe 
those who break the law

00:15:03.110 --> 00:15:06.660
must be punished appropriately.

00:15:10.880 --> 00:15:11.970
Punished?

00:15:12.350 --> 00:15:14.060
Let's see...

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:20.480
Perhaps I'll have you throw a banquet 
soon, paid for by the Mononokean.

00:15:22.950 --> 00:15:24.660
What? A banquet?

00:15:28.230 --> 00:15:31.620
A human who used his influence to kill yokai...

00:15:35.540 --> 00:15:37.420
How horrifying.

00:15:41.190 --> 00:15:44.500
Yeah. Yahiko wasn't lying.

00:15:45.270 --> 00:15:50.320
When we talked about it before, 
you didn't seem that interested.

00:15:50.320 --> 00:15:52.430
Why did you ask to see Sakae's form?

00:15:52.430 --> 00:15:53.510
Let's go.

00:16:00.440 --> 00:16:02.520
<i>What's his problem?</i>

00:16:11.460 --> 00:16:13.530
<i>He's definitely hiding something.</i>

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:16.530
<i>But I rejected his offer to look into it,</i>

00:16:17.190 --> 00:16:19.290
<i>so I can't press him too hard.</i>

00:16:27.620 --> 00:16:29.510
I do sense something.

00:16:30.980 --> 00:16:32.050
Over there!

00:16:34.180 --> 00:16:35.590
After him, Fuzzy!

00:16:37.200 --> 00:16:39.060
Fuzzy, go!

00:16:51.160 --> 00:16:52.730
Please excuse us.

00:16:52.730 --> 00:16:54.200
We thought you were running.

00:16:54.200 --> 00:16:56.950
Don't worry about it.

00:16:57.570 --> 00:17:01.200
You're humans, but you can see me.

00:17:01.200 --> 00:17:03.440
I forgot to introduce myself.

00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:06.250
I'm Abeno, master of the Mononokean.

00:17:06.570 --> 00:17:09.210
We're his employees, Ashiya and Fuzzy.

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:10.910
The Mononokean?

00:17:10.910 --> 00:17:14.360
The Mononokean that exorcises 
yokai to the Underworld?

00:17:14.360 --> 00:17:16.410
Yes, that Mononokean.

00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:19.370
Oh, perfect timing!

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:23.220
I've been wanting to go to the Underworld.

00:17:23.910 --> 00:17:27.850
In that case, we'll exorcise 
you the day after tomorrow.

00:17:28.550 --> 00:17:30.730
Wait for us in front of the torii gate.

00:17:31.750 --> 00:17:32.860
Got it.

00:17:33.540 --> 00:17:35.210
See you later, Bonta-san.

00:17:35.640 --> 00:17:38.380
See you later, Ashiya.

00:17:38.380 --> 00:17:40.150
Mononokean, come.

00:17:44.830 --> 00:17:47.830
Welcome back!

00:17:48.250 --> 00:17:49.460
We're back.

00:17:52.550 --> 00:17:55.460
Golden hair and eyes...

00:17:55.460 --> 00:17:56.550
Is that...

00:18:12.380 --> 00:18:14.980
<i>So the exact whereabouts</i>

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:20.340
<i>and fate of the yokai 
he banished are unknown.</i>

00:18:23.750 --> 00:18:27.290
If they're still banished,

00:18:27.290 --> 00:18:30.180
it's possible they could still be saved.

00:18:32.470 --> 00:18:34.800
I'm home, Brother.

00:18:34.800 --> 00:18:36.510
Welcome back, Shizuku.

00:18:36.510 --> 00:18:38.950
You seem busy with work.

00:18:39.360 --> 00:18:42.010
I'll make some tea. Give me a minute.

00:18:42.010 --> 00:18:43.880
Hooray.

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:01.120
What are you doing?

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:02.530
Cleaning the brush.

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:07.000
Did you talk to those Abeno and Ushiya boys?

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:09.550
It's Ashiya, Dad.

00:19:09.550 --> 00:19:12.280
They said it should go 
away in a couple of days.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:13.800
I see.

00:19:15.630 --> 00:19:17.090
Ow!

00:19:17.420 --> 00:19:19.820
Well, that's good.

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:22.060
This isn't a monster movie.

00:19:22.060 --> 00:19:25.500
Though it's not inconceivable that 
a spider monster might be there.

00:19:25.500 --> 00:19:27.400
What? A spider?

00:19:27.400 --> 00:19:28.890
Didn't I tell you?

00:19:29.240 --> 00:19:31.900
You only mentioned the red eyes.

00:19:31.900 --> 00:19:35.690
Apparently there's a giant 
spider with one red eye there.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:38.980
Wh-What a ridiculous story.

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:48.730
<i>He was a cute yokai that looked like a pig.</i>

00:19:49.520 --> 00:19:51.240
<i>His eyes weren't red, either.</i>

00:19:54.230 --> 00:19:55.520
<i>That's odd.</i>

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:57.620
Zenko, my tail!

00:19:56.680 --> 00:19:58.170
Oh, sorry.

00:20:01.640 --> 00:20:03.580
What is it, Zenko?

00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:05.380
Just physical affection between family.

00:20:44.710 --> 00:20:47.770
Finally, finally...

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:50.820
Please, help.

00:20:51.970 --> 00:20:53.370
Help me.

00:20:55.520 --> 00:20:57.110
Hey!

00:20:57.840 --> 00:20:59.610
Bonta-san!

00:21:04.240 --> 00:21:05.710
I wonder what happened.

00:21:05.710 --> 00:21:08.620
Do you think he forgot we were 
meeting in front of the gate?

00:21:08.620 --> 00:21:11.130
I can sense Bonta-dono.

00:21:11.130 --> 00:21:13.050
Should we split up and look for him?

00:21:13.050 --> 00:21:14.010
Yeah.

00:21:14.480 --> 00:21:16.810
I'll check behind the shrine.

00:21:23.080 --> 00:21:25.840
He toyed with his own power,

00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:28.640
eventually committing a 
taboo in the mundane world,

00:21:30.150 --> 00:21:32.420
banishing a yokai.

00:21:38.230 --> 00:21:42.270
<i>I sensed another yokai for 
a moment the other day.</i>

00:21:46.870 --> 00:21:47.780
What's wrong?

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:50.730
Abeno-san, come quickly!

00:21:50.730 --> 00:21:51.530
Hurry to—

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:40.020
<b>Next Time: "True Intentions"</b>

00:23:25.840 --> 00:23:28.630
Something's wrong with our client Bonta-san.

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:31.180
What? Now there's something wrong with me.

00:23:31.180 --> 00:23:33.640
Watch out, Abeno-san and Fuzzy!

00:23:34.050 --> 00:23:35.760
Next time, "True Intentions."

00:23:36.080 --> 00:23:38.220
Who's there?
